# Frontend design quality

Before building a substantial screen, load `.skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` and the licensed `.skills/anthropic-frontend-design/SKILL.md` when available.

Then:
1. Identify user goals, primary action and expected information hierarchy.
2. Read `docs/brand.md` and any supplied visual references. Use EmpressVR's navy, magenta, green and cosmic visual character deliberately.
3. Pick a coherent layout rhythm, typography scale, responsive behavior and interaction states.
4. Use generous spacing, purposeful contrast, reusable patterns and readable line lengths. Avoid generic dashboard cards, arbitrary gradients, excessive decorations and repetitive "AI-generated" visuals.
5. Check color contrast, keyboard navigation, mobile clipping, loading and error states.
6. Compare a browser screenshot with the intended design and revise if possible. Report visual verification status honestly.
7. Preserve accurate content and labels from the client. Placeholders remain clearly marked until migration.

Prioritize clarity and distinct brand identity over visual trends. Reference: https://github.com/anthropics/skills/tree/main/skills/frontend-design
